course: dictionary
lesson: 9844
title: Words that turn
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To swivel means to turn round on one spot, like turning in a chair or turning your head quickly. Only the turning part moves; the rest stays in place. «Every tank holds a different survival trick: a mantis swivels its head to stare at you.» The mantis does not walk round to look at you. Its head turns on the spot.
explain: Look for clues around the word. The word «stare» tells you the head is turning to look at something, so swivel must mean turn. Check by swapping in your meaning: «a mantis turns its head to stare at you» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Swivel can also be a noun or an adjective. A swivel is a joint or part that lets something turn round while staying in place, and a swivel chair is an office chair that can turn round. Watch the endings: swivels, swivelled and swivelling all come from the same word.
fact: Swivel means to turn round on one spot.
fact: «A mantis swivels its head to stare at you.» The head turns, and the body stays still.
fact: A swivel is a joint or part that lets something turn round while staying in place.
fact: A swivel chair is an office chair that can turn round; children can spin on one safely, but should never stand on it.
fact: Swivel is spelt swiveled in American English and swivelled in British English.
exercise: «Jumping spiders hunt by sight with two big front eyes, and their main eyes can swivel inside the head.» What does swivel mean here? | To shrink to nothing | To jump high into the air | *To turn round on one spot | To close tightly
exercise: A swivel chair is an office chair that does what? | Hisses loudly | *Turns round | Flies up into the air | Glows under ultraviolet light
exercise: Find and copy one word from «a mantis swivels its head to stare at you» that means turn round on one spot. | head | *swivels | stare | mantis
test: Ella says a swivel is a joint. What does a swivel do? | Holds water | *Lets a part turn round while staying in place | Makes a sound like a whistle | Pulls two things apart
test: What does swivel mean in «A chameleon's two eyes can swivel separately»? | *Turn, each one on its own | Grow longer every day | Blink very quickly | Close shut at night
exam: Jayden says swivel means to jump up and down. What does swivel really mean? | *To turn round on one spot | To fall over | To go to sleep | To jump up and down
